    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full test suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 2/2 tests). The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the registration-date rule for `POST /api/owners`: when no `registrationDate` is supplied it defaults to the server's current date, and the owner's `registrationDate` is returned in ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` format.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `registrationDate` field (`type: string, format: date`, optional) to the `OwnerFields` schema. Being in `OwnerFields`, it flows into both the request DTO (`OwnerFieldsDto`) and response DTO (`OwnerDto`, via `allOf`), and MapStruct auto-maps it by name. `format: date` generates a `LocalDate`, which Jackson serializes as `YYYY-MM-DD` (same as the existing Pet `birthDate`).\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added the `registrationDate` (`LocalDate`) field mapped to a `registration_date DATE` column, with getter/setter.\n\n3. **`BuildOwner.java`** \u2014 after mapping the request to an `Owner`, defaults `registrationDate` to `LocalDate.now()` when it's null; a supplied date is preserved.\n\n4. **DB schemas** \u2014 added the nullable `registration_date DATE` column to the `owners` table in all four schema files (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres). The column is nullable so existing `data.sql` seed inserts remain valid.\n\nBoth acceptance tests pass: `coreDefaultsToToday` (no date supplied \u2192 today) and `functionalityKeepsSuppliedDate` (supplied `2020-06-15` preserved).",
